[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDagent/main/docs/assets/brand/banner.png[/img][/center]

[center][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]An assistant inside Night City that writes, runs, checks and fixes your mods with you while you play.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center][size=3]REDagent is a chat window over Cyberpunk 2077, powered by Claude. Ask it about your mods, their logs and the game; ask it to make a mod, and it writes it, watches it load, reads its log and fixes what is wrong. It runs on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url] and uses your own Anthropic API key.[/size][/center]

[center][size=3]What changed in each version: [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDagent/changelog.html]changelog[/url] · Guide: [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDagent/guide.html]REDagent guide[/url][/size][/center]

[line]

[quote][size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]STATUS: PREVIEW[/color][/b][/size]
Built in the open and tested in the game after every phase, now on [b]game version 2.5[/b].
[b]You pay Anthropic for what you use[/b], with your own API key. A Claude.ai subscription cannot be used.[/quote][line]

[color=#19f3ff][i][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35670/35670-1792883384-1285424381.png[/img][/i][/color]
[color=#19f3ff][i][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35670/35670-1792883396-1270068791.png[/img][/i][/color]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What you can ask[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]"What's in my mod log?"[/b] It reads REDnode's Mod log, crashes included, and explains them.[/*]
[*][b]"What are V's health, level and money?"[/b] It looks the game functions up and reads them from the running game.[/*]
[*][b]"What does this mod's window show?"[/b] It captures the overlay window and reads it.[/*]
[*][b]"What's on my screen?"[/b] It takes a picture of the game when it needs to see, with or without REDnode's windows.[/*]
[*][b]"Make a mod that warns me when V's health drops below 30%."[/b] It writes a new REDnode mod, waits for it to load, checks it runs and fixes it.[/*]
[*][b]"Swap my changed archive into the game."[/b] It swaps it into the running game through REDnode, so a changed mesh or texture shows without a restart.[/*]
[/list]It cannot press keys or move the mouse in the game, run commands or install packages.
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35670/35670-1792883407-2089624677.png[/img]


[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]You stay in control[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Every file change is shown first[/b] as a diff, added lines in green and removed in red: [b]Allow[/b], [b]Allow all in this chat[/b] or [b]Deny[/b].[/*]
[*][b]Every change has Undo.[/b] REDagent backs up each file before it changes it.[/*]
[*][b]It writes only in REDnode's apps folders[/b], never its own files, never a node_modules folder, nowhere else on your PC.[/*]
[*][b]It asks you before every call that could change your game[/b] (money, health) and before every archive swap. Reads never ask. Quest changes and moving V are not available to it.[/*]
[*][b]Each answer shows its cost[/b], with the chat's running total.[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Mods can ask it too[/color][/b][/size]

Other mods can ask REDagent questions and show you the answers, for example a mod that explains an error. Only once you allow it, only to read (never to change your files or game), on Sonnet 5.5, within a daily spending limit per mod ($0.25 unless you change it), and with pictures off unless you switch them on for that mod.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url] 0.38.1 or later, with what it needs (RED4ext, redscript).[/*]
[*]Your own [b]Anthropic API key[/b]: [url=https://console.anthropic.com/]console.anthropic.com[/url], under API keys. Anthropic bills you for what you use.[/*]
[*]Anthropic's [b]Claude Agent SDK[/b], which REDagent runs on: REDagent downloads it at first start (below).[/*]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 on PC, Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, [b]game version 2.5[/b]. For game 2.31, use REDagent 0.3.1 from this page's archived files, with REDnode 0.37.0.[/*]
[*]About 300 MB of disk, and about 120 MB of memory while the game runs.[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] Mod Manager Download, then enable and deploy. Install REDnode first.[/*]
[*][b]By hand:[/b] extract the zip into the game folder, so REDagent lands in [i]red4ext/plugins/REDnode/apps/redagent/[/i].[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]First run[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Start the game. The REDagent window opens on the right. Press [b]Get the Agent SDK[/b] and wait for it to finish.[/*]
[*]Press [b]F10[/b], open the [b]Mod Manager[/b] at the top of the REDnode launcher and select REDagent. Switch [b]Allowed[/b] on for "REDnode's tools for AI agents", so it can see the game and your mods' logs.[/*]
[*]Paste your API key into REDagent and press [b]Save key[/b]. The chat appears.[/*]
[*]Ask something short, like "What's in my mod log?"[/*]
[/list][color=#19f3ff][i][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35670/35670-1792883416-123641503.png[/img][/i][/color]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]The Claude Agent SDK[/color][/b][/size]

REDagent runs on Anthropic's Claude Agent SDK. The SDK is Anthropic's and not open source, so it is not in this download. [b]Get the Agent SDK[/b] fetches Anthropic's own packages from npm (a pinned version, about 140 MB), checks each against npm's integrity hash, and unpacks them into REDagent's data folder on your PC. A download that fails or does not match is thrown away. Its use is subject to [url=https://code.claude.com/docs/en/legal-and-compliance]Anthropic's terms[/url].

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Your key and your data[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Your API key[/b] is stored encrypted with your Windows account, by REDnode, used only to talk to Anthropic, and never shown again.[/*]
[*][b]Your questions, REDagent's answers and what it reads to answer[/b] (mod logs, game values, pictures it takes, the files it reads) are sent to Anthropic's API, as with any Claude API use.[/*]
[*][b]Everything else stays on your PC.[/b] REDagent sends no telemetry.[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What it costs[/color][/b][/size]

You pay Anthropic per use, and each answer shows what it cost. [b]Opus 5.5[/b] (the default) is for writing and fixing mods; [b]Sonnet 5.5[/b] is for quick questions at a lower price. In our first test, six questions cost $0.34 in all. A long chat costs more per question, since the whole chat is sent each time: start a [b]New[/b] chat when you change topic.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Questions[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Can I use my Claude.ai subscription?[/b]
No. Anthropic does not allow claude.ai logins in third-party products, so REDagent uses an API key, billed per use.

[b]It says REDnode's tools are off.[/b]
Press F10, open the [b]Mod Manager[/b], select REDagent and switch [b]Allowed[/b] on.

[b]Get the Agent SDK failed.[/b]
Check your connection and press it again. A partial download is thrown away, never used.

[b]Is it free?[/b]
REDagent is free and open source under the MIT license. Claude is not: you pay Anthropic for what you use.

